WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.430
We've all thought about disasters, imagined
massive floods, fires, or a meteor crashing

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:07.600
into Earth.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:13.300
But what happens when the destruction comes
quietly and suddenly, with the dawning of

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:14.620
a new day?

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:20.210
Over the next 24 hours, the world as we all
know it will crumble, and something strange

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:23.310
and terrible will rise to take its place.

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:24.700
What will that look like?

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.800
Who will try to rise to the occasion and help,
and who will cower in the dark?

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:35.579
What happens to the people around the world
in the first 24 hours after Day Breaks?

00:00:35.579 --> 00:00:36.819
Let's find out.

00:00:36.819 --> 00:00:37.819
Hour 1

00:00:37.819 --> 00:00:42.840
It's 6 AM on a farm in Kansas, and the land
is just beginning to wake up.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:47.219
The farmer and his wife and children are still
sleeping, waiting for the cry of their rooster

00:00:47.219 --> 00:00:49.929
to tell them that it's time to start the day.

00:00:49.929 --> 00:00:55.129
The cows are grazing in the open field, letting
out the occasional half-hearted "moo," but

00:00:55.129 --> 00:00:57.710
they're still a bit too sleepy to give it
their all.

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:01.819
The pigs snort restlessly in the barn, feeling
breakfast time approaching.

00:01:01.819 --> 00:01:06.240
The rooster, proud and stately, hops onto
the roof of the chicken coop, surveying his

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:07.240
domain.

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:10.110
He tilts his head back and lets out a mighty
crow.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:16.280
Cock-a-doodle...the sound catches in his throat
as something strange begins to happen.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:19.840
His beak softens, like wax dripping from a
lit candle.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:25.170
It drops to the ground with a soft plop as
his mighty wake-up call fades to a gurgle.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:30.799
There is something wrong this morning, something
truly, deeply wrong.

00:01:30.799 --> 00:01:34.590
If the rooster were capable of complex thought,
he would be terrified.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:40.680
Instead, he is just melting, along with the
hens, the cows, and the pigs, all dripping

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:44.729
onto the grass as the faint light of morning
changes them.

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:48.940
Inside the farmhouse, the family begins to
scream.

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:49.940
Hour 2

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:54.829
An hour later, in New York City, the city
that never sleeps gets a rude awakening.

00:01:54.829 --> 00:01:59.719
No one can be sure when exactly the chaos
broke out, but all of a sudden people in their

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:05.479
little apartments wake to the sound of masses
of people calling out for help, of the thunderous

00:02:05.479 --> 00:02:11.410
footsteps of crowds tearing through the streets,
and then...of a strange gurgling sound that

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:13.030
replaces the bedlam.

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:18.390
A young woman throws open her blackout curtains
to get a better look, and finds herself melting

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:20.440
along with them.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:24.911
Across town, a landlord knocks on his tenant's
door, demanding some overdue rent, but there

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:26.560
is no answer.

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:30.910
Only the slop of something oozing across the
floor inside.

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:36.030
Security footage of Times Square catches an
eerie sight, masses of molten flesh spreading

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:41.160
across the streets, the masses of tourists
that were gathered there only hours before

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:47.840
melted together into something else, bathed
in the neon glow of the billboards and lights

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:49.260
of the city.

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:50.310
Hour 3

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:54.660
On the other side of the world, in Canberra,
Australia, a group of college students is

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:55.950
camping in the wilderness.

00:02:55.950 --> 00:03:00.940
While the United States is waking up to a
horror show, they are sleeping soundly in

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:03.320
their tents beneath the light of the moon.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:08.260
Well, except for one of them, who had decided
to take his sleeping bag outside and sleep

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:09.490
under the stars.

00:03:09.490 --> 00:03:14.560
That would have been a lovely idea, except
for the fact that all sunlight, including

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:20.480
that which reflected off the moon, has become
quite destructive to the human body.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:22.950
To all living things, in fact.

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:28.020
His melted form sloshes around inside the
sleeping bag, trying to regain some semblance

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:30.000
of its original shape.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.570
Inside their tent, his friends are still themselves,
shielded remarkably well from the light by

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:36.740
the thick canvas.

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:41.850
That is, until one of them gets up to go to
the bathroom, and unzips the front of the

00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:42.850
tent.

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:47.070
His mouth is already useless by the time he
thinks to scream, and the moonlight floods

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:50.860
inside and covers the group in a silvery glow.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:55.040
It doesn't take long for them to meet the
same fate as their friend outside, melting

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:57.690
together into one massive entity.

00:03:57.690 --> 00:04:04.780
They had hoped this camping trip would bring
them closer together, and, well...it did.

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:05.780
Hour 4

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:12.180
Meanwhile, a speleologist is deep in the bowels
of a cave in Tian Shan that she has been studying,

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.950
completely unaware of the terrors of the surface.

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:19.290
She's taking samples, dictating notes to her
research assistant, and keeping an eye out

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:24.640
for bats, when suddenly, she receives a communication
from one of the members of her research team

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:25.730
up above.

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:29.880
The technology they use only allows for short
text messages that can be transmitted through

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:35.760
the layers of soil and rock all around, but
this warning needs only a few words: "Don't

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:36.830
come up.

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:38.490
Not safe."

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:41.370
The words send a chill up her spine.

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:45.560
What could possibly be happening that's more
dangerous than being down here?

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:50.130
She writes back, asking for clarification,
but receives none.

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:55.310
Through the dark tunnels, illuminated only
by a few headlamps, she thinks she can hear

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:57.710
the echo of a scream.

00:04:57.710 --> 00:04:59.020
Hour 5

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:03.460
Those that are still safe, and have managed
to hold onto their identities and forms, have

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:07.310
noticed yet another threat in addition to
whatever the light is doing.

00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:12.690
All around the world, planes are dropping
from the sky, their pilots and crews transformed

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:15.930
into something incapable of flying an aircraft.

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:20.680
Airplanes that were en route to their various
destinations, thousands of them going in every

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:26.821
direction imaginable, are now plummeting toward
the ground, crashing into the ocean, or, in

00:05:26.821 --> 00:05:34.170
some especially unlucky cases, landing on
buildings that still have survivors inside.

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:39.200
It's a truly brutal bit of irony, to escape
the sun's terrible rays and find some small

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:44.240
sanctuary, only to have a plane fall out of
the sky and destroy it all.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:45.900
Hour 6

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:51.460
Over at the SCP Foundation, everyone is on
high alert, trying to categorize what is happening

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:53.290
and find a way to stop it.

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:58.650
But how do you contain an anomaly when that
anomaly is the sun itself?

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:03.150
In the meantime, the O5 Council retreats to
a specialized underground bunker constructed

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:08.530
especially for this kind of dire scenario,
outfitted with beds, reading materials, and

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:14.180
enough supplies to keep them alive for several
years, as long as no one hogs the snacks.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:18.010
As the rest of the Foundation staff scramble
to find a solution before the rest of the

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:22.110
Earth's population is reduced to goo, the
anomalies contained throughout the various

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:25.340
sites begin to take notice.

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:30.870
SCP-999 oozes frantically around its site,
hugging and nuzzling anyone it can get close

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:31.870
to.

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:35.650
It doesn't fully understand what is going
on, but it can tell that everyone is quite

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:40.580
upset and frightened by something, and it
wants to help them feel better.

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:44.010
Other anomalies have a less charitable approach.

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:49.610
SCP-173 takes advantage of the chaos to escape
containment, snapping a few necks on its way

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:51.250
out just for fun.

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:54.130
After all, everyone's eyes are otherwise occupied.

00:06:54.130 --> 00:07:00.170
Because it is not made from any organic material,
it is immune to the effects of the sun, and

00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:03.680
makes its way outside to explore the pandemonium.

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:08.520
Research staff that pass by SCP-682's containment
chamber can hear the giant beast chuckling

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:14.560
to itself, a sickening, choking sound as it
laughs at the fall of humanity.

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:15.560
"Finally..."

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:16.770
It sighs.

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:20.910
One scientist peeking in through the observation
window swears that the hard to destroy reptile

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:26.380
is smiling, before one of his colleagues ushers
him down the hall, away from the monster's

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:27.760
celebration.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:33.790
SCP-507 appears in the hall with a pop, back
from another one of his involuntary inter-dimensional

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:34.790
voyages.

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:36.080
"Woah, where's the fire?"

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:39.250
He asks, taking in the hysteria around him.

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:41.050
"Did something get out?"

00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:43.420
A bit of unease creeps into his voice.

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:44.420
"No!"

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:45.420
Shouts a passing guard.

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:47.120
"It's what's trying to get in."

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:48.120
"God!

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:50.340
I have the worst timing!"

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:51.410
507 groans.

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:52.470
Hour 7

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:56.760
Back in the realm of civilians, newscasters
hop on to broadcast from studios devoid of

00:07:56.760 --> 00:08:01.530
natural light, unsure if there are any survivors
left to hear their messages.

00:08:01.530 --> 00:08:06.470
One television personality forces his usual
bright smile, staring down the barrel of the

00:08:06.470 --> 00:08:09.480
camera with barely-concealed tears in his
eyes.

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:12.860
He can't let his smile crack, can't let himself
break down.

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:18.900
If he lets himself cry, really cry, he's scared
he won't be able to stop.

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:21.040
"Please remain calm."

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:25.380
He reads off the teleprompter, as a production
assistant sobs into the shoulder of the camera

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:26.380
operator.

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:29.750
"Experts are working to determine what is
going on.

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:36.180
In the meantime, please follow these instructions
to ensure your safety, and that of your loved

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:42.199
ones: Do not go outside, unless you are covered
in proper equipment to shield yourself from

00:08:42.199 --> 00:08:44.089
the sun or moon.

00:08:44.089 --> 00:08:47.529
Block all sources of natural light in your
residence.

00:08:47.529 --> 00:08:52.649
Do not attempt to interact with those who
have been affected by this disaster, do not

00:08:52.649 --> 00:08:57.119
touch them, do not let them into your home,
do not speak to them.

00:08:57.119 --> 00:08:59.390
Again, please remain calm.

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:00.390
Help is on the way."

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:05.019
He doesn't know if the words are true, he
only knows that it's his responsibility to

00:09:05.019 --> 00:09:10.550
give the people hope, something familiar they
can turn to when nothing makes sense.

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:12.199
The camera switches off.

00:09:12.199 --> 00:09:15.379
He covers his face and lets the tears loose.

00:09:15.379 --> 00:09:16.379
Hour 8

00:09:16.379 --> 00:09:20.720
In spite of the pleas from newscasters, people
are very much panicking.

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:21.970
How could they not?

00:09:21.970 --> 00:09:26.699
Everything's descended into absolute mayhem
and it's only been eight hours since it all

00:09:26.699 --> 00:09:27.699
began.

00:09:27.699 --> 00:09:32.399
Unfortunately, where there is panic, there's
someone trying to make a quick buck off of

00:09:32.399 --> 00:09:34.139
their fellow man.

00:09:34.139 --> 00:09:38.589
Even more unfortunately, the internet is still
up and running so far, and with survivors

00:09:38.589 --> 00:09:43.040
taking to social media to livetweet their
experiences and post as much as they can on

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:48.760
Instagram, Facebook, and anywhere else they
can reach out for help, it's the perfect environment

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:49.899
for scammers.

00:09:49.899 --> 00:09:54.360
A Twitter thread goes viral, claiming that
wrapping oneself in aluminum foil will protect

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:56.220
against the effects of the light.

00:09:56.220 --> 00:10:01.160
Facebook posts circulate, hawking all sorts
of natural remedies and "super sunscreens"

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:03.610
from essential oil blends to bacon grease.

00:10:03.610 --> 00:10:08.829
A fraudulent GoFundMe page pops up, claiming
to belong to a climate scientist raising money

00:10:08.829 --> 00:10:13.579
for a ray gun that will reverse the damage
done to the Earth's atmosphere, which he cites

00:10:13.579 --> 00:10:15.860
as the cause of the destruction.

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:16.949
Hour 9

00:10:16.949 --> 00:10:20.079
Not all of the information circulating online
is false, however.

00:10:20.079 --> 00:10:24.800
A video is posted on TikTok with the caption
"these mofos can TALK!!!!!"

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:29.529
featuring video of a teenage boy cowering
in a dark room as one of the formerly human

00:10:29.529 --> 00:10:32.990
flesh creatures moves around outside the door.

00:10:32.990 --> 00:10:38.209
After a moment or two of silence, a garbled
voice calls out to him "Brian...come outside...please,

00:10:38.209 --> 00:10:46.399
come out into the sun...I miss you..."

00:10:46.399 --> 00:10:50.639
The video's comments are filled with other
users sharing similar experiences, saying

00:10:50.639 --> 00:10:52.790
"It talked just like my boyfriend!"

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:58.649
"It barked like a dog!" or even "It was singing
my favorite Ariana Grande song."

00:10:58.649 --> 00:11:03.300
Similar videos pop up in the wake of this
first recording, urging survivors to ignore

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:07.629
the voices, no matter who they seem like they
belong to.

00:11:07.629 --> 00:11:08.629
Hour 10

00:11:08.629 --> 00:11:12.449
While some people are using the internet to
spread helpful information on the nature of

00:11:12.449 --> 00:11:17.679
the events outside, others have ruled out
rational explanations entirely, claiming that

00:11:17.679 --> 00:11:23.220
this is a divine punishment for the sins of
mankind, or the Matrix finally collapsing

00:11:23.220 --> 00:11:24.699
in on itself.

00:11:24.699 --> 00:11:27.889
Others deny that the horrible events are even
happening at all.

00:11:27.889 --> 00:11:33.360
An infamously contrarian Livestream personality
logs on from his insulated basement, crowing

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:36.389
to his viewers that "None of this is actually
happening.

00:11:36.389 --> 00:11:39.959
It's all a ploy to keep us complacent and
under government control.

00:11:39.959 --> 00:11:43.179
As yourself, why don't they want us going
outside?

00:11:43.179 --> 00:11:45.709
So we don't see what they're really up to."

00:11:45.709 --> 00:11:48.660
As commenters try desperately to change his
mind, he doubles down.

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:50.499
"You're all a bunch of sheeple.

00:11:50.499 --> 00:11:51.499
Baa!

00:11:51.499 --> 00:11:52.499
Baa!"

00:11:52.499 --> 00:11:53.499
He laughs.

00:11:53.499 --> 00:11:54.499
"Look, I'll show you that there's nothing
to worry about."

00:11:54.499 --> 00:11:58.459
He carries his laptop upstairs with him, and
steps outside onto the sidewalk.

00:11:58.459 --> 00:12:02.370
In his computer screen, he can see the video
feed of his own face beginning to droop and

00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:05.059
liquefy before he can even feel it.

00:12:05.059 --> 00:12:10.160
He tries to run back inside, away from the
light, but it's too late.

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:11.989
His legs are already giving out.

00:12:11.989 --> 00:12:17.249
The viewers can only watch as their favorite
streamer dissolves in real-time, until his

00:12:17.249 --> 00:12:22.819
now-useless hands drop the laptop to the ground,
where it breaks into pieces, and the stream

00:12:22.819 --> 00:12:24.240
goes dark.

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:25.259
12

00:12:25.259 --> 00:12:29.060
For those who have survived this long, at
the 12-hour mark, things are beginning to

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:30.060
get tense.

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:33.009
Actually, that would be an understatement.

00:12:33.009 --> 00:12:37.410
Tensions have been bubbling steadily for the
past twelve hours as people have melted into

00:12:37.410 --> 00:12:43.199
unrecognizable waxy monsters, exploded in
plane crashes, and been traumatized to within

00:12:43.199 --> 00:12:44.899
an inch of their lives.

00:12:44.899 --> 00:12:47.920
Now, those tensions are boiling over.

00:12:47.920 --> 00:12:53.179
Human beings in a crisis can be a bit like
crabs in a bucket, vicious and ready to tear

00:12:53.179 --> 00:12:57.380
each other to pieces if they perceive that
they might be left behind.

00:12:57.380 --> 00:13:03.749
When there is a shortage of resources, this
selfish fear and anger only get worse.

00:13:03.749 --> 00:13:05.089
Hour 13

00:13:05.089 --> 00:13:09.369
There might not be a lack of food or fresh
water yet, but there is another resource that

00:13:09.369 --> 00:13:13.019
seems worth destroying each other for: darkness.

00:13:13.019 --> 00:13:17.739
In a world where light means death, the only
safe place is in the dark.

00:13:17.739 --> 00:13:21.279
But there are a limited number of places that
people can go.

00:13:21.279 --> 00:13:26.550
In rural areas, families retreat to storm
cellars or the insides of empty grain silos.

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:31.309
In cities, underground parking garages become
hiding places, and there just isn't enough

00:13:31.309 --> 00:13:33.689
space there to go around.

00:13:33.689 --> 00:13:38.089
People erupt into physical fights in these
parking complexes, punching and shoving each

00:13:38.089 --> 00:13:42.819
other, even attacking with broken bottles
and other improvised weapons, all to stake

00:13:42.819 --> 00:13:46.319
their claim over this newfound territory.

00:13:46.319 --> 00:13:51.329
Even more contentious are warehouses, insulated
hiding places filled with all of the supplies

00:13:51.329 --> 00:13:57.629
that will soon start to dwindle: toilet paper,
canned goods, soap, and bottled water.

00:13:57.629 --> 00:14:03.309
These things just might be worth killing for,
and many are already prepared to do so.

00:14:03.309 --> 00:14:04.309
Hour 14

00:14:04.309 --> 00:14:08.509
While the SCP Foundation is busy trying to
maintain order and find a way to end this

00:14:08.509 --> 00:14:13.339
catastrophic event, other groups dedicated
to the anomalous are equally busy.

00:14:13.339 --> 00:14:18.199
The Chaos Insurgency attempt to launch a sneak
attack on Site-19 while its occupants are

00:14:18.199 --> 00:14:19.199
distracted.

00:14:19.199 --> 00:14:23.389
However, their defenses against the sun prove
ineffective, and they are melted before they

00:14:23.389 --> 00:14:26.360
can so much as reach the Site's entrance.

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:29.529
Inside, the Foundation staff never even notice.

00:14:29.529 --> 00:14:32.709
They've got far too much on their hands already.

00:14:32.709 --> 00:14:36.959
Other groups take a less offensive approach,
prioritizing safety.

00:14:36.959 --> 00:14:41.059
Members of the Serpent’s Hand escape to
the interdimensional Wanderer's Library along

00:14:41.059 --> 00:14:45.829
with their families, settling in for the long
haul and preparing to make it their permanent

00:14:45.829 --> 00:14:48.139
home as the Earth burns.

00:14:48.139 --> 00:14:52.589
They didn't want it to end this way, but they're
not going to stick around to be a part of

00:14:52.589 --> 00:14:53.699
it all.

00:14:53.699 --> 00:14:55.199
Hour 18

00:14:55.199 --> 00:14:59.139
Not all people are turning on each other,
even as things appear dire.

00:14:59.139 --> 00:15:03.369
The best thing anyone can do in a horrible
situation is to look for those willing to

00:15:03.369 --> 00:15:05.059
extend a helping hand.

00:15:05.059 --> 00:15:10.051
There will always be people trying to look
out for others, to put out the fires, and

00:15:10.051 --> 00:15:12.490
airlift people out of the flood waters.

00:15:12.490 --> 00:15:18.750
Though this disaster seems anything but natural,
the instinct to help is still there for many.

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:23.089
Doctors and nurses hole up in hospitals, blocking
out the windows with spare pairs of scrubs

00:15:23.089 --> 00:15:26.230
and whatever else they can find to light-proof
the building.

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:30.899
There, they treat the wounded that make it
inside, wrapping broken bones and stitching

00:15:30.899 --> 00:15:32.929
up wounds as best they can.

00:15:32.929 --> 00:15:37.540
A few well-intentioned souls even attempt
to treat those changed by the sun, those things

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:42.339
that barely look human anymore, no matter
how hard they try to arrange their soft bodies

00:15:42.339 --> 00:15:44.459
back into their former shape.

00:15:44.459 --> 00:15:46.470
It's too late for them, though.

00:15:46.470 --> 00:15:50.360
There's nothing to be done, and no medical
school in the world could have prepared a

00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:52.189
doctor to heal this hurt.

00:15:52.189 --> 00:15:55.489
But what about the people who aren't all the
way gone?

00:15:55.489 --> 00:16:00.769
The ones who started to change, but got inside
in time to slow, or even stop, the process?

00:16:00.769 --> 00:16:05.990
Hospital staff treat the melting like an infection,
amputating molten limbs or attempting to clean

00:16:05.990 --> 00:16:10.759
and bandage them, unsure of what to do with
a piece of the human body that no longer behaves

00:16:10.759 --> 00:16:12.339
like flesh and bone.

00:16:12.339 --> 00:16:17.029
They're able to save a few people, but far
more are already doomed by the time they make

00:16:17.029 --> 00:16:18.670
it inside.

00:16:18.670 --> 00:16:23.970
They disintegrate slowly, but steadily, fading
away on the operating table until their warbling

00:16:23.970 --> 00:16:27.329
voices are urging the doctors to follow them
outside.

00:16:27.329 --> 00:16:29.600
"It doesn't hurt..."

00:16:29.600 --> 00:16:34.339
They promise, reaching out with fleshy tentacles
that once were hands.

00:16:34.339 --> 00:16:38.559
It's hard to remember the Hippocratic oath
when a monster is trying to pull you into

00:16:38.559 --> 00:16:39.980
its grasp.

00:16:39.980 --> 00:16:40.980
Hour 20

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:45.089
While some are trying to help the creatures
created by the sun's wrath, others have been

00:16:45.089 --> 00:16:49.119
waiting for this moment since they saw their
very first zombie movie.

00:16:49.119 --> 00:16:54.759
To them, this is an outbreak, plain and simple,
and it's the perfect chance to suit up and

00:16:54.759 --> 00:16:56.290
play soldier.

00:16:56.290 --> 00:17:00.799
They cloak themselves in body armor and helmets
with dark tinted visors, and grab whatever

00:17:00.799 --> 00:17:02.569
weapons they can find.

00:17:02.569 --> 00:17:08.100
Grenades, firearms, flamethrowers, anything
is fair game at the end of the world.

00:17:08.100 --> 00:17:12.370
A former police officer and massive fan of
zombie-themed first-person shooters takes

00:17:12.370 --> 00:17:17.750
to the streets, staring down an enormous mound
of flesh made from dozens of people melding

00:17:17.750 --> 00:17:22.439
together, ropy tentacles flailing and grasping
for more bodies to add to its mass.

00:17:22.439 --> 00:17:27.589
He fires an array of bullets into the thing,
but they are absorbed into its surface, swallowed

00:17:27.589 --> 00:17:28.789
up inside.

00:17:28.789 --> 00:17:34.720
He searches for weak points, for eyes, a heart,
anything he can target, but he can't spot

00:17:34.720 --> 00:17:36.380
anything vulnerable.

00:17:36.380 --> 00:17:38.960
But he's not deterred, he'll try fire next.

00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:43.610
He lights a homemade Molotov cocktail and
hurls it at the beast, waiting for it to ignite

00:17:43.610 --> 00:17:46.510
and listening for the sound of its painful
cries.

00:17:46.510 --> 00:17:47.840
But nothing comes.

00:17:47.840 --> 00:17:53.460
The cocktail explodes, and nearby debris catches
on fire, but the ball of flesh doesn't react.

00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:59.140
It just continues to advance toward him, making
its way down the street as if it has all the

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:00.690
time in the world.

00:18:00.690 --> 00:18:04.440
There's only one option left, and it's the
riskiest one of all.

00:18:04.440 --> 00:18:07.110
He pulls out a grenade, and pulls the pin.

00:18:07.110 --> 00:18:11.889
Throwing it won't do, he needs to run up and
thrust the grenade into the body of the monster,

00:18:11.889 --> 00:18:13.529
to blow it up from inside.

00:18:13.529 --> 00:18:15.710
He's going to have to be quick.

00:18:15.710 --> 00:18:19.130
He summons all of the stamina from his high
school track and field days and makes a mad

00:18:19.130 --> 00:18:22.529
sprint for the creature, holding the grenade
out in front of him.

00:18:22.529 --> 00:18:25.240
Eyes on the prize, there is nothing but the
mission now.

00:18:25.240 --> 00:18:27.130
The chance to be a hero.

00:18:27.130 --> 00:18:31.769
He is so singularly focused on his task, that
he doesn't notice a tentacle snaking along

00:18:31.769 --> 00:18:37.590
the ground toward him until it loops around
his feet, flipping him over until he's upside

00:18:37.590 --> 00:18:38.590
down.

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:41.669
The force of the movement knocks his helmet
loose, and it falls to the ground below.

00:18:41.669 --> 00:18:45.080
He moves to shield his face with his hands,
but it's useless.

00:18:45.080 --> 00:18:46.789
The sunlight has already found him.

00:18:46.789 --> 00:18:51.519
He is already changing, becoming one with
the very thing he promised to destroy.

00:18:51.519 --> 00:18:56.309
He stares up at the mass with reverence, just
before his eyes drop out of his head, and

00:18:56.309 --> 00:18:58.980
reaches his arms out to welcome its embrace.

00:18:58.980 --> 00:19:03.039
By the time the grenade detonates, he can't
bring himself to care about it.

00:19:03.039 --> 00:19:07.519
He can't care about anything, except being
a part of the flesh.

00:19:07.519 --> 00:19:08.789
Hour 22

00:19:08.789 --> 00:19:13.260
If individuals have a tendency to blame each
other in times of strife, then governments

00:19:13.260 --> 00:19:15.000
are even worse.

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:19.179
Surviving leaders of various countries, shivering
in their bunkers and tearing out their hair

00:19:19.179 --> 00:19:24.179
with stress, begin to convince themselves
that this must be some kind of act of biological

00:19:24.179 --> 00:19:26.080
warfare gone wrong.

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:29.470
Nuclear testing, some kind of deadly gas,
something.

00:19:29.470 --> 00:19:33.620
Surely, ruination on this grand of a scale
must be man-made.

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:38.399
With no other recourse, they begin declaring
war on each other, everyone pointing a finger

00:19:38.399 --> 00:19:42.230
at someone else as no one is able to take
responsibility.

00:19:42.230 --> 00:19:47.789
The threats, the denials, and the rage escalate
until finally, the North Korean government

00:19:47.789 --> 00:19:52.690
makes a decision that would seem completely
insane under any other circumstances: they

00:19:52.690 --> 00:19:55.830
attempt to nuke the sun.

00:19:55.830 --> 00:20:00.620
It's irrational, and it's ineffective, of
course, but it's the last gasp of a species

00:20:00.620 --> 00:20:03.010
hurtling toward extinction.

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:08.510
One final attempt to bring it all to an end,
before it's all truly over.

00:20:08.510 --> 00:20:09.890
Hour 24

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:15.639
And as the dust clears, it becomes completely
apparent: the old world is dead.

00:20:15.639 --> 00:20:21.370
And a new world, for better, or for much,
much worse, is born.

00:20:21.370 --> 00:20:24.390
Nothing will ever be the same again.

00:20:24.390 --> 00:20:31.981
Now go check out "SCP-001 When Day Breaks
Dr Bright" and "When Day Breaks SCP-035" for

00:20:31.981 --> 00:20:33.990
more of everyone’s favorite apocalypse!

